  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The method relies on dominant image colors as a proxy for actual material reflectance, which may introduce inaccuracies compared to direct physical measurements.",
      "what": "The researchers developed a Python 3.10 program that estimates urban surface albedo by extracting dominant colors from street-view images and mapping them to reflectance values. Applying this tool to the densely built Kowloon District in Hong Kong, they mapped spatial variations in albedo and identified lower albedo values in the southern parts of the district due to a concentration of dark-colored surfaces.",
      "why": "It provides a highly scalable, low-cost method for mapping urban albedo across complex street canyons using existing street-level imagery, replacing expensive and localized physical measurement campaigns."
    }
